+# Task 9 downstream empty-schema helper — prepared, not executed
+
+This is root coordination preparation only. The adjacent Python helper has not been executed, and no Task 9 schema, private env, grant, migration, test, model, or product change was made by this preparation. Task 7 remains the sole product author. Root must wait for actual Task 7 adoption, repin the Task 9 source and migration prefix, review the exact helper bytes and this note, and only then decide whether to run the helper. Root separately issues an application ACK after observing the created empty schema; the Task 9 author then performs its normal 15-resource bootstrap.
+
+The helper uses the existing bounded Task 8 MySQL container only: full CID `11009a6b34fef0416e651100fbde05a07067dbcbd973f1ba731c08b2281140ad`, honest name `/ama-test-task08-848e93aace8b4f0fa34fc548267f3dc5`, owner label `task08-848e93aace8b4f0fa34fc548267f3dc5`, pinned MySQL 8.4.6 image, loopback port 44727, InnoDB/AIO 0, server UUID `1bdea6eb-cf32-11f1-8fe3-fef4aa4b3a25`, 768 MiB memory and swap, 1 CPU, 256 PIDs. It verifies selected Docker fields and both before and after SQL server identity against the recorded parent guard and Task 7 root ACK. It does not request another container, network, credential, PKI, or S3 resource. It never uses the older shared 46653 fixture or a fake legacy container name.
+
+At future execution, root chooses **one** fresh UUID and passes `task09-<32 lowercase hex>` plus `ama_t09_<first 12 hex>_behavior`. The helper refuses an existing owner path or schema. It verifies the private `.tools` paths, uses the existing Task 8 mounted `root.cnf` and `test.cnf`, and makes only the new empty schema and its grant to the existing Task 8 test principal. It parses the root-created Task 7 env as literal assignments with `shlex`, without sourcing or evaluating it. It accepts only the known Task 7 keys, then writes a Task 9 allowlist env: `AMA_TEST_DATABASE_{URL,USERNAME,PASSWORD}`, exact `AMA_TEST_CONTAINER`, and `AMA_TASK09_{OWNER,RUN_ROOT,S3_ENV,PKI_ROOT}`. The URL points only to the new Task 9 schema; the existing test username/password and S3/PKI reference values are carried unchanged in memory. No Task 7 or Task 8 schema URL is copied. The new env is `0600` in the fresh `0700` owner directory. It never prints, hashes, or places secret values in command arguments or records. The only SQL mutations are the recorded `CREATE SCHEMA` and scoped `GRANT`; no migration, business write, reset, `DROP`, `clean`, `repair`, or `outOfOrder` operation is present.
+
+The explicit execution flag, approved helper SHA-256, Task 7 adoption evidence path and SHA-256, and scoped names are all required. Root should use the exact helper hash from the adjacent manifest after independent static review. The adoption evidence argument is a rooted, hash-checked handoff reference; root must verify that it is an actual completed adoption record, because the helper cannot infer adoption semantics from an arbitrary file. An illustrative future command shape, with values supplied only after those checks, is:
+
+```sh
+python3 .superpowers/sdd/2026-10-23-ama-phase-b-remaining/task-09-fixture-provisioning-prepared-20261024.py \
+  --execute-reviewed-task9-provisioning \
+  --approved-helper-sha256 '<reviewed helper SHA-256>' \
+  --task7-adoption-evidence '<actual Task 7 adoption record within tree>' \
+  --task7-adoption-sha256 '<that record SHA-256>' \
+  --owner 'task09-<fresh 32 lowercase hex>' \
+  --schema 'ama_t09_<same first 12 hex>_behavior'
+```
+
+The helper records selected-before fields, server/version/AIO/engine/UUID, `partial_revokes=0`, SQL mode without `NO_BACKSLASH_ESCAPES`, schema absence, and the exact nonsecret creation SQL in private `state.json` **before** issuing SQL. The `CREATE SCHEMA` identifier is the literal new name; the database-level `GRANT` pattern escapes every underscore so it grants that exact schema under MySQL 8.4's [GRANT pattern rules](https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/grant.html). For example, `ama_t09_0123456789ab_behavior` grants on `` `ama\_t09\_0123456789ab\_behavior`.* ``. It records phases after schema creation and grant, then verifies selected-after fields and zero tables and writes the private env. Any failure preserves the owner path and an honest partial/unknown status; root must inspect state and actual database outcome. Do not rerun with another UUID to hide an uncertain first attempt, and never drop or clean the partial result. A successful helper result still requires root's separate application ACK before author bootstrap.
+
+Static preparation here used only source reading, AST parse, and structural checks. Docker, MySQL, private file values, JVM, product source, tests, index, and Git state were not touched.
